<title>SINGAPORE: SML nets US$6 mln from tug deal.</title>
<headline>SML nets US$6 mln from tug deal.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sembawang Maritime Ltd (SML) said on Tuesday it had raised US$8.9 million from the sale of a tug and supply boat as part of the rationalisation of its marine salvage and transportation operations.</p>
<p>The sale of the 10,000 BHP &quot;Salviceroy&quot; would result in a pre-tax gain of about US$6.0 million after commission and expenses, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>It said the transaction was due to be completed on Wednesday when full payment would be made on delivery, subject to the vessel's passing of standard inspections, surveys and repairs.  </p>
<p>Proceeds would be used to repay existing loans and fund acquisitions.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703011)</p>
